**Read:** [Physical Geology, second edition — Steven Earle](../sources/Physical-Geology-Earle.lingua#r_5GWEYVQGR176TXMQT0S881ZSKX), chapter 20 in full; [Geodiversidade do Brasil — Cassio Roberto da Silva and contributors](../sources/Geodiversidade-do-Brasil.lingua#r_2ZQN8TT3KZYS9MCFGZV5A1V682), the complete mineral/material-resource treatment; [Mineral Commodity Summaries 2026 — USGS](../sources/Mineral-Commodity-Summaries-USGS.lingua#r_47FJ4GZC4CS4KJX8WXNDB418CX), overview, definition appendices, and the complete selected commodity chapters.

Geological resources include water, aggregates, dimension stone, industrial minerals, metals, energy-bearing materials, and other useful geological attributes. Their formation, distribution, accessibility, quality, variability, and interactions differ. A material can be common in the crust while deposits meeting a particular specification are scarce or difficult to use.

Concentration can involve magmatic, hydrothermal, sedimentary, weathering, biological, metamorphic, or reworking processes and combinations across time. A deposit model connects evidence and process; it is not a guarantee that every matching regional setting contains an extractable body. Mineral occurrence, exploration target, resource estimate, reserve, and operating supply are distinct claims under identified definitions.

Grade, tonnage, mineral form, grain association, contaminants, location, water, power, transport, and recovery influence usefulness. High bulk abundance does not guarantee a separable or sufficiently pure feedstock. A semiconductor material's final specifications are downstream requirements that geology alone cannot establish.

**Work:** read the whole resource chapter and the statistical report overview/definitions. Choose copper, silica, or another infrastructure material; compare two deposit settings and explain implications for sampling, processing, and waste. Trace actual edition/units and distinguish geological inventory, mine production, refining, trade, and manufacturing capacity in the report.

Continue later into the dedicated mineralogy/petrology, economic geology, mining, beneficiation, refining, and manufacturing subjects. Their unique work remains substantial; this shared geological route supplies the material/history foundation and a clear statement of what remains unknown.

**Continue:** [Investigate the subsurface with traceable samples, observations, and alternatives](Exploration-drilling-and-subsurface-models.lingua#r_0EEXNVK4NWE8G3HC3XH9QSSBCA).

